  "finalReply": "Done. The current board is contradictory (no consistent mine placement), so the correct output is `-1,-1`.\n\n**Analysis of `/app/board.txt`:** the `1` at `(4,5)` forces `(3,6)=mine`, which via `(3,5)=1` forces `(2,4),(2,5),(2,6)=0`, via `(3,4)=1` forces `(2,3)=mine`, via `(3,3)=1` forces `(3,2),(4,2)=0`, via `(4,3)=1` forces `(5,2)=mine`, via `(6,3)=1` forces `(7,3),(7,4)=0`, via `(6,4)=1` forces `(7,5)=mine` — but `(5,5)=1` forces `(6,6)=mine` and `(6,5)=1` then forces `(7,5)=0`. Contradiction, hence invalid.\n\n**Solution (`/app/main.py`, run via `python3 main.py`):**\n- Parses/validates 16×16 board (`.` / `0`-`8`); outputs `-1,-1` if no unrevealed cells or invalid.\n- Builds constraints `sum(adjacent unknowns) = number` per revealed cell; immediate invalid if `req<0` or `req>unknowns`.\n- Splits frontier into connected components, exact backtracking enumeration (≤28 vars) with constraint propagation, randomized sampling + single-solution probe + naive fallback for larger components.\n- Returns a cell with mine-count 0 in all exact solutions if one exists (provably safe, priority 1).\n- Otherwise ranks frontier by marginal mine probability with exact global reweighting under assumed 40 mines (log-domain hypergeometric weighting over component mine-count distributions), estimates interior as `(40-E[frontier])/N_interior`, picks the minimum; handles assumption violations and ties.\n- Writes `row,col` to `/app/safe_move.txt`.\n\n**Verification:** `python3 main.py` on the given board outputs `-1,-1`; spot-checked valid boards (single `0` → adjacent safe, single `1` → frontier min, `8` → interior win, full/malformed/bad-char → `-1,-1`, random simulated valid board) all return correct-format unrevealed cells quickly.",
